# FrontendAI OS is a browser-only app — nothing in the dependency tree needs a
# native build step, so install scripts are disabled. This keeps the single
# `npm install` identical on Windows, WSL, Linux and macOS.
#
# What this skips, and why it is safe:
#   onnxruntime-node  postinstall downloads a ~100 MB native binary from
#                     api.nuget.org. It is only reachable through
#                     @huggingface/transformers' "node" export condition
#                     (dist/transformers.node.mjs). Vite resolves the "default"
#                     condition to dist/transformers.web.js, which uses
#                     onnxruntime-web (WASM) — the built transformers.web-*.js
#                     chunk contains no reference to onnxruntime-node or sharp.
#   protobufjs        postinstall only prints a message; the package is pure JS.
#
# Every platform binary this project actually needs (rolldown, sharp, esbuild)
# ships inside optionalDependencies tarballs, so those install correctly with
# scripts disabled — npm picks the right one for the host OS/arch automatically.
#
# Delete this line if you ever add a dependency that must compile at install time.
ignore-scripts=true
